        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Rain within the first hour usually means a recoat. Rain after several warm, dry hours usually means nothing worse than a few spots that fade. Everything in between depends on what you see once the drive has dried completely, so wait a full day, inspect in good light, and test suspect patches before deciding.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            To avoid a repeat, plan around a block of at least 24 dry hours, seal in the morning, switch off sprinklers, and never cover fresh sealer with plastic. A good weather window does more for the finish than any product upgrade.
          </p>
        </div>

